- When the user confirmed while the preview was still running, the
  preview kept running and interleaved with the deletion. Now, the
  preview is stopped when the user confirms. #bug
- Prevent cleaner reload and worker running simultaneously. OTA
  winapp2.ini update or closing the preferences dialog could interrupt
  a preview or cleaning in progress: registration empties the cleaner
  list while the worker still reads it, which throws errors. #bug
- Refuse to delete if another operation starts during the
  confirmation. Example: user clicks delete, the confirmation
  appears, and a background OTA winapp2.ini update refreshes the
  cleaner list. #bug
- Prevent shredding files or wiping empty space while the worker is
  busy. They could be triggered by the application menu or
  drag-and-drop. The race condition had potential side effects such
  as the abort button cancelling only one of the two operations. #bug
- If the worker fails to start, re-enable the window and hide the
  progress bar. #bug
- Fix a race in "Shred Settings and Quit" when "Exit after cleaning"
  was enabled. The application exited before rebuilding the minimal
  configuration file: either the old settings were written back
  (settings restored), or the clean file was never written (no file).
  In portable mode, the missing file makes the next launch behave
  like installed mode and write settings to the user profile. #bug
- Enforce delete confirmation for shredding when expert mode is off,
  even if confirmation was previously disabled. This prevents a
  bypass if the user enables expert mode, disables delete
  confirmation, then turns expert mode back off. #bug
- Stop the operation when the window is closed. #bug
- Do not ask to confirm deletion when a drag-and-drop contains no
  valid files, which can happen when dragging from the Linux
  trash. #bug
- Skip relative paths when shredding plain text from the clipboard.
  (The clipboard feature originates in 253019af to fix issue #303.)
  #bug
- If the user toggled an option with a warning that raced with a
  cleaner reload, the wrong option could be toggled instead. #bug
- When the user clicked an option with a warning but did not accept
  it (cancelled the dialog, or it was blocked by Expert Mode), the
  parent checkbox became checked even though no child was enabled.
  #bug
- Prevent a hung or slow update check from keeping the process
  running after the window closes. #bug

Behavior changes:
- --gui paths now opens a separate instance when one is already
  running instead of dropping the paths. Users will see two windows.
- bleachbit --gui --no-delete-confirmation paths without expert mode
  will now prompt.
- Windows context menu to shred files will prompt, unless expert mode
  is enabled and delete confirmation is disabled.
